    },
    {
      "section_id": "SEC038",
      "title": "The Real Cost of the Doctrine",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "In the time of Jesus, people lived under Roman military occupation. A Roman soldier could compel any passerby to carry his pack for one mile, simply by right of conquest. You are not who you think you are to resist such a demand; think of it like asking who Anguissa is in that position of forced compliance. And Jesus said, when a soldier tells you to go one mile, go two miles with him.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA146",
            "EX023",
            "SRC003919",
            "SRC003922",
            "SRC003925",
            "SRC003938",
            "SRC003940",
            "SRC003941"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC003919",
            "SRC003922",
            "SRC003925",
            "SRC003938",
            "SRC003940",
            "SRC003941",
            "SRC003966",
            "SRC003970",
            "SRC003974"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA146"
          ],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX023"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000011",
          "provider_handle": "p11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Think of it like meeting a colonial tutor who was also a colonel. He looks at your shirt and says, I like that shirt. For him to say that he likes it means you must give it to him. You do not ask questions when he says it. And Jesus taught that you should go and get the suit you bought the shirt with, and give him two of them as well.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA146",
            "EX024",
            "SRC003949",
            "SRC003960",
            "SRC003963",
            "SRC003966",
            "SRC003967",
            "SRC003970",
            "SRC003971",
            "SRC003974"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC003949",
            "SRC003960",
            "SRC003963",
            "SRC003966",
            "SRC003967",
            "SRC003970",
            "SRC003971",
            "SRC003974",
            "SRC003919",
            "SRC003938",
            "SRC003940",
            "SRC003941"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA146"
          ],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX024"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000012",
          "provider_handle": "p12"
        },
        {
          "text": "These two illustrations, the soldier and the tutor, show what Jesus' teaching actually cost the people who first heard it.",
          "kind": "connective",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA146"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC003919",
            "SRC003938",
            "SRC003940",
            "SRC003941",
            "SRC003966",
            "SRC003970",
            "SRC003974"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA146"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000013",
          "provider_handle": "p13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Do not imagine that the doctrine of Jesus was an easy one. They slap you on one cheek, you give them the other. That was Jesus' doctrine, given under real, harsh occupation, not as a comfortable abstraction.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA147",
            "SRC003978",
            "SRC003981",
            "SRC003984"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC003978",
            "SRC003981",
            "SRC003984"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA147"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000014",
          "provider_handle": "p14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sometimes when we are teaching, if we don't look at the Bible carefully, we reach for modern illustrations, democracy, freedom of speech, and when we think in those categories we behave in a certain way that can misrepresent the biblical reality underneath the text if Scripture itself is not checked.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA148",
            "SRC003986",
            "SRC003988",
            "SRC003992",
            "SRC003994",
            "SRC003995"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC003986",
            "SRC003988",
            "SRC003992",
            "SRC003994",
            "SRC003995"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA148"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000015",
          "provider_handle": "p15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Today, nobody forces you to come to church. You can identify with a congregation and then withdraw without needing to inform anyone. At most, your pastor might decide that your conduct is too much for the fellowship. This was not always so; church attendance and tithing were once enforced by civil and religious authority rather than left to voluntary participation.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA149",
            "SRC003996",
            "SRC003999",
            "SRC004003"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC003996",
            "SRC003999",
            "SRC004003",
            "SRC004035",
            "SRC004038",
            "SRC004050"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA149"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000016",
          "provider_handle": "p16"
        },
        {
          "text": "There is a place in America called West Virginia where, by report, the pastor will call the police for you if you do not pay your tithe. Other American pastors have reported that if a man drives past the church on a Sunday, playing music, they call the police on him, saying, this man is a troublemaker.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA149",
            "EX025",
            "SRC004033",
            "SRC004035",
            "SRC004038",
            "SRC004041",
            "SRC004042"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004033",
            "SRC004035",
            "SRC004038",
            "SRC004041",
            "SRC004042",
            "SRC003996",
            "SRC003999",
            "SRC004003",
            "SRC004050"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA149"
          ],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX025"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000017",
          "provider_handle": "p17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Even in Switzerland, when they ask which church you are going to, a portion of your income, ten percent, is sent there directly. Even in Germany it is the same.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA149",
            "EX026",
            "SRC004047",
            "SRC004049",
            "SRC004050",
            "SRC004052"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004047",
            "SRC004049",
            "SRC004050",
            "SRC004052",
            "SRC003996",
            "SRC003999",
            "SRC004003",
            "SRC004035",
            "SRC004038"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA149"
          ],
          "example_refs": [
            "EX026"
          ],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000018",
          "provider_handle": "p18"
        },
        {
          "text": "How did they kill Jesus? Religious authorities came disguised as those concerned with right doctrine, saying he does not agree with our religion, and political authorities colluded with them. Politicians said, we are going to tell the president, and Pilate simply washed his hands quickly. Historically, religious and political power collaborated to execute those who dissented, as happened with Jesus.",
          "kind": "substantive",
          "evidence_handles": [
            "IDEA150",
            "SRC004009",
            "SRC004013",
            "SRC004015",
            "SRC004019",
            "SRC004023",
            "SRC004025"
          ],
          "source_refs": [
            "SRC004009",
            "SRC004013",
            "SRC004015",
            "SRC004019",
            "SRC004023",
            "SRC004025"
          ],
          "idea_refs": [
            "IDEA150"
          ],
          "example_refs": [],
          "reference_refs": [],
          "uncertainty_refs": [],
          "paragraph_id": "P000019",
          "provider_handle": "p19"
        }
      ],
